                  <origin>
                     <origDate when-custom="140X/141X" notBefore="1400" notAfter="1419" calendar="#gregorian">s. xv in.</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#i"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_30">Barking, Essex. Abbey
                        of St Mary the Virgin and St Ethelburga, of Benedictine nuns</orgName><p>'Iste liber constat domine Sibille de Felton', Abbatisse de
                        Berkyng' (fol. 4v, at end of table of chapters); 'Mistris Agnes Gowldewell'
                        me possidet ex dono Margarete Scroope quondam monache monasterii de
                        Berckynge' (fol. 175v, s. xv/xvi).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Medieval binding, faded pink leather over
                     bevelled boards.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">'Mystris Gowldewell me possidet teste
                     streete' (fol. 170v, s. xvi in.)</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">On first pastedown are: 'John Campe owe this
                     booke'; 'Reinold Clarke is the trewe owner of this Booke' (s.
                     xvi).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">'Henry Elmy' and date 1620 (fol.
                     84v).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">'Bought of Roger Pott of Colechester
                     Bookseller the 29th of Aprill 1628. Payde for it xis vid' (second
                     pastedown).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Belonged in 1944 to Mr Frank Brown,
                     historian, then to Messrs Maggs, London.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Sold at Sothebys 19 July 1949, lot 276, to Mr
                     William Foyle (1885–1963) of Beeleigh Abbey, Maldon (Essex), passed by
                     inheritance to daughter Christina Foyle (1911–1999).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Sold, Foyle Sale at Christie's, 11 July 2000,
                     lot 72, to Sam Fogg.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Now in an American collection.</provenance>
               </history>
